# network.target — the network setup has run (slinit-services). A daemon
# that needs the network says `depends-on: network.target` or, if it
# copes without it, `waits-for: network.target`, rather than naming
# the service that configures it. Reached even when that service fails
# (no cable, no DHCP server), so it does not take its dependents down.
type = internal
depends-on: local.target
waits-for: network
